  "body_html": "<h1>Normal Form Reduction</h1>\n<p>The normal form reduction of a perfect-information extensive game is the map\n$$\n  F:\\prod_{i\\in I} S_i\\to R\n$$\nthat sends each pure strategy profile to the unique terminal outcome it induces.\nComposing $F$ with terminal payoff functions gives an ordinary strategic game in\nnormal form.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Definition 6.2.1] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. The normal or strategic form reduction associates each strategy profile to its induced outcome.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
